==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Test}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɛstə/}}
* {{rhymes|ɛstə(r)}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|testre}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|testa}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[canopy]] over a [[bed]] etc.
#* '''1851''', Herman Melville, ''Moby-Dick'':
#*: With our shaggy jackets drawn about our shoulders, we now passed the Tomahawk from one to the other, till slowly there grew over us a blue hanging '''tester''' of smoke, illuminated by the flame of the new-lit lamp.

===Etymology 2===
From {{suffix|test|er}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A person who administers a [[test]], or a [[device]] used for testing.
# {{Australia|slang|obsolete}} 25 [[lash]]es, ie. strokes of a [[whip]] across a person's back as a punishment.  (Reference: [[w:Robert Hughes (critic)|Robert Hughes]], ''[[w:The Fatal Shore|The Fatal Shore]]'', 1987, paperback 1996 ISBN 1-86046-150-6, chapter 12.)
# A [[sample]] of perfume available in a shop for customers to try before they buy.

